{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792897945,"nonce":"oCxpPDdnw+eaPaoUMQlaP0NkV4E=","target":"5b76cfb1940ca6c191aa2831b965c6d853cd5ab03ecd8e654621916196134c0b","message":"The benchmark's rayzor-tiered compile column (parse, TAST, MIR prep, startup passes, module load; stdlib setup excluded) was 87-118 ms on 8 of 12 kernels with the full O2 pipeline run before the program started.\n\nMeasured on the NUC (Alder Lake), embedded snapshot valid, `~/tiered_ct.sh` (benchmark_runner --targets rayzor-tiered), two passes:\n\n| kernel | after (ms) |\n|---|---|\n| binarytrees | 39-43 |\n| deltablue | 30 |\n| fannkuchredux | 41-46 |\n| fasta | 41-43 |\n| knucleotide | 45-47 |\n| pidigits | 46-47 |\n| regexredux | 45-48 |\n| revcomp | 45-48 |\n| spectralnorm | 40 |\n| fibonacci, mandelbrot, nbody | 5-13 |\n\nPer-kernel baselines were not recorded; before, 8 of 12 were 87-118 ms. Intermediate: O2 deferred alone gave 57-66 ms.\n\nWhat moved it (sampled with pprof-rs via SIGPROF, since perf_event is blocked on the NUC):\n- Benchmark harness now matches `rayzor run`: PassManager::startup() before main, the rest of O2 deferred to the first native compile.\n- startup() runs one pipeline round instead of up to five.\n- A cached import already indexed by discovery is not re-parsed.\n- register_method_from_blade scanned the whole symbol table per method when no manifest index was active (every per-import cache restore): 28% of compile time. Now looks up symbols by simple name.\n- BLADE decodes of all discovered imports run in parallel after discovery (sequential ~10 ms -\u003e ~5 ms; threads contend, worth revisiting).\n- fixup_stale_cross_module_refs builds bare-name candidates only for names it will look up.\n- take_mir_modules moves the merged module out instead of deep-cloning it (CLI and harness).\n- A stale project artifact no longer shadows a valid embedded snapshot: it falls through to the next source and is deleted (first run after a compiler rebuild was 230+ ms from relowering the stdlib).\n\nRemaining per-kernel cost (revcomp, ~45 ms): import registration ~13 ms, user-file lowering ~13 ms (stdlib merge 4.5, monomorphize 2.7), tree shake ~5 ms, startup passes ~5 ms (InsertFree twice ~2.6, inlining ~1.9), cross-module fixup ~4 ms (instruction walk over every import module), prefetch ~5 ms.","files":null}]}